{"id": "EUVD-2026-75111", "enisaUuid": "e9a51f26-d245-37f3-b237-91678a3d407f", "description": "MaxSite CMS through 109.6 ships with a hardcoded session encryption key in application/config/config.php that is never changed during installation, allowing unauthenticated attackers to forge administrator session cookies. Attackers can mint a malicious ci_session cookie with administrator privileges by computing an HMAC-SHA1 using the publicly known encryption key, bypassing authentication checks in is_login() and mso_check_allow() functions.", "datePublished": "2026-09-09T16:45:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:21:31", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/maxsite/cms", "https://github.com/EviL0rd/maxsite-cve4/blob/main/2026.09.08-maxsite-cms-hardcoded-session-key-auth-bypass.md", "https://github.com/maxsite/cms/blob/2ca0a0c7d1d71106a25dbb0f2aedaaefbf12802c/application/config/config.php#L230-L254", "https://github.com/maxsite/cms/blob/2ca0a0c7d1d71106a25dbb0f2aedaaefbf12802c/application/maxsite/common/core/init.php#L70-L96", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/maxsite-cms-through-109.6-authentication-bypass-via-hardcoded-encryption-key"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-87929", "GHSA-x43r-8q5x-82p8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.53, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "827a5cd4-2355-39aa-b219-f4d4d785bd40", "product": {"name": "MaxSite CMS", "vendor": {"name": "MaxSite"}}, "product_version": "0.78 \u2264109.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4bf3f7b8-253d-3311-8e10-1bf08620a685", "vendor": {"name": "MaxSite"}}], "isExploited": false}